<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to March 29.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to March 29.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to March 29 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week March 23-March 29</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,607,347 tns	187,601 tns    11.67 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,893,258 tns	218,573 tns    11.54 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,757,409 tns	199,541 tns    11.35 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to March 29</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    27,295,011 tns    2,946,831 tns    10.80 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    26,926,526 tns    2,874,867 tns    10.68 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    25,517,167 tns    2,693,580 tns    10.56 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during week, 59 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 60 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 59 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
</text>
